Rule 1 (size as tuple: length matches rank and fits within value shape; suppresses “Need value.shape >= size” and negative begin)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len = ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2.len ≥ 1 ∧ ∀ i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : 0 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] ≤ shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 2 (size as tensor: must be 1-D int32/int64 and length equals rank(value); suppresses incompatible-shape and begin/size rank errors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4) ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (value must be at least 1-D with all positive dimensions; helps avoid invalid slice ranges)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ if ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 then ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 else false
>>
Rule 4 (seed is non-negative; uses union over primitive types)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (name is a valid operation name from the allowed set)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = "none" ∨ v_1 = "valid" ∨ v_1 = "same" ∨ v_1 = "channels_last" ∨ v_1 = "channels_first"
>>
Rule 6 (value must not have string-like dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 7 (common image case: if channels dimension exists, do not crop it)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if v_2.len = ndim(v_1) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 then ∃ i ∈ [ndim(v_1) - 1, ndim(v_1) - 1] : v_2[i] = shape(v_1, i) ∨ v_2[i] = 1
